{"id": "DDQ-RRP-0040", "question": "Do donor-facing tax disclosures and acknowledgments reflect the 2025 amendments to IRC 170 by Pub. L. 119-21, including that the new deduction for donors who do not itemize excludes contributions to donor-advised funds?", "category": "RRP", "subcategory": "Tax disclosure currency", "business_concern": "Donor-facing tax content must track changes in the law it describes.", "risk_addressed": "Donors are told, or led to believe, that a DAF contribution qualifies for the non-itemizer deduction.", "source_refs": [{"source_id": "SRC-IRC-170", "relation": "maps-to", "basis": "directly-documented"}], "industries": ["donor-advised-funds", "nonprofit"], "jurisdictions": ["US-federal"], "products": ["unbound"], "regulatory_authority": "IRS", "requirement_classification": "industry-convention", "customer_importance": "high", "answer_unit": "ANS-RRP-002", "answer_scope_note": "ANS-RRP-002 already requires that tax disclosures never imply non-itemizer deductibility. The 0.5 percent floor added by Pub. L. 119-21 affects donors' own deduction calculations, which Unbound does not compute.", "controls": ["ECTL-RRP-003", "ECTL-RRP-004", "ECTL-RRP-005"], "requirements": ["UNB-RCN-FIN-001", "CNV-FIN-003", "UNB-RCN-WF-004", "UNB-RCN-ENT-009", "RR-UNB-ACC-006-r1", "UNB-DOC-002", "UNB-RCN-FIN-015", "UNB-RCN-PLT-007", "UNB-RCN-PLT-010", "RR-REQ-X-032-r1", "UNB-RCN-FIN-012", "UNB-RCN-GRT-015"], "evidence_requirements": ["EVR-RRP-002"], "disclosure_classification": "nda", "history": [{"date": "2026-11-25", "change": "created (stale-reference sweep: IRC 170 amended by Pub. L. 119-21)", "by": "refinement-agent"}]}
